{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1018139-who-can-be-a-demiurge","id":1018139,"title":"Who can be a Demiurge?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-16T10:22:35-08:00","id":1018139,"title":"Who can be a Demiurge?","content":"I've been thinking about a pair of NPC's for my setting, one of whom has brought the other back from the dead. I originally thought of making the returned one a vampire, but then I thought of making the character a Promethean. Now I realize that the Created hardly if at all remember who the bodies were they were formed from, but I wonder - could a mage or an occultist be a demiurge? Could such a character act as demiurge to, say, an ulgan? If this question has already been answered somewhere, I apologize, I onlyown the 1st edition core bok.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/373-infernal-teddy","name":"Infernal Teddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar373_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T10:35:23-08:00","id":1018144,"title":"","content":"Yes, a mage or occultist can be a demiurge. In the 1e supplement Saturnine Night, it was explained that mages had to forego using magic in order to be a demiurge, and that successfully creating a Promethean put their connection to the Supernal at risk. 2e doesn't say anything about what happens to the demiurge, but says that the resulting Promethean is an Extempore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T10:58:42-08:00","id":1018146,"title":"","content":"Two things:<br /> <br /> 1. I have always hypothesized that Isis, the wife of Osiris and Progenitor of the Osiran Lineage, is a Thyrsus, and Inanna, the lover of Tammuz and Progenitor of the eponymous Lineage, was a Moros (I say was because I also believe she eventually transformed into a vampire and became the founder of the Daeva clan).<br /> <br /> 2. Magical Traditions, in the section on Kabbalism, states that a mage with Matter 5 and Mind 5 can create a self-willed &quot;golem,&quot; basically a Promethean made out of inanimate matter (I guess you would call it an Unfleshed in 2e terms). I believe that is exactly what Tammuz was--as a Moros, Matter 5 and Mind 5 would not have been out of the question for Inanna, given that she was powerful enough to be worshipped by the ancient Sumerians as a goddess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T10:59:41-08:00","id":1018147,"title":"","content":"Substitute Life 5 for Matter 5 (as would be appropriate for a Thyrsus), and you have a regular Promethean--i.e. Osiris.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T11:10:19-08:00","id":1018150,"title":"","content":"Have fun with it in your games; but that's not how things work according to the rules as written. Note that Mage 1e's Tome of the Mysteries included a section on Alchemy which included rules for creating artificial beings; those beings were not Prometheans. They weren't animated by Azoth and weren't on a Pilgrimage. Mage 2e hasn't yet addressed the subject of Supernal Alchemy; but it looks like it might in the upcoming Signs of Sorcery supplement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T11:37:46-08:00","id":1018156,"title":"","content":"Facts of 2E games are those:<br /> 1. ANYBODY can be Demiurge, being able to channel Pyros - if creator is not typical genitor or human obsessed with Linage sources ( like rabbi with 'Jews golems' on Tammuz ), end result will probably be Extempore.<br /> 2. Mages <b>cannot</b> directly, operate on Pyros Alchemy. They <i>maybe</i> make some modifications or changes to process, but those are limited. Azoth very much don't like Supernal Magic.<br /> 3. Mages <i>can</i> create autonomic artificial servants - just see <i>Golem</i> spell in Matter 4 of 2E <b>Mage</b> corebook.<br /> <br /> Ergo, Awakened sorcerer can create 'robot' by Supernal Magic, but it will never start Pilgrimage on it's own. Or rather, if it will get Azoth, it will by blind choice of Principle ( i.e. Alchemical Gods ). Isis or Innana could be even Archmages by wizards standards, it does not change fact they cannot just 'spell' being to life. Only the will of Azoth and striking of Pyros can give real symbalance of life to previous 'robot'. / And I very like this scenraio, to you information. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> /<br /> <br /> If you want to know more on relations between Created Alchemy and mages Supernal Magic in 2E - I point you to the<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945024-2e-prometheans-and-mages\"> topic on this very idea</a>, in Mage forums. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T12:16:45-08:00","id":1018169,"title":"","content":"I don't understand. Isn't any self-willed artificial being a Promethean, the same way any blood-drinking undead being is a Kindred?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T12:23:41-08:00","id":1018173,"title":"","content":"Wrong on both counts. There are self-willed artificial beings that aren't Prometheans, and there are blood-drinking undead beings that are not Kindred. The V1e supplement Wicked Dead gives some examples of the latter.<br /> <br /> More generally, do not assume that any given gameline portrays every type of classical monster that its protagonists are based on. Vampire deals with the Kindred, not every kind of vampire; Werewolf deals with the Uratha, not every werewolf; Mage deals with the Awakened, not every mage; and so on. Some come closer to having a monopoly than others; you're not going to find many changelings who aren't the Lost, but there are at least four known kinds of beings called demons, of which the Unbound are but one.<br /> <br /> ChroD supernatural types are representative, but not definitive; it's always possible to find exceptions or alternatives, because the premise is that it's never possible to know everything that's out there in the shadows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 12-16-2016, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T12:45:36-08:00","id":1018186,"title":"","content":"Why can't a sufficiently powerful mage imbue a corpse or a statue with Azoth (or Pyros--are they the same thing?) and <br /> make it a Promethean? Why in the world would you want to limit your Demiurge pool to people who DON'T have occult powers? Especially with a game system like Chronicles of Darkness, which encourages crossovers to begin with? Just wondering...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":11905,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","user":"JulianMoon","date":". 12-16-2016, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T12:58:52-08:00","id":1018191,"title":"","content":"It was established in an early Mage supplement that magic can't normally mess with most supernatural power or fuel stats, be it a Kindred's Blood Potency or Vitae, an Uratha's Primal Urge or Essence, or a Promethean's Azoth or Pyros. Short of archmastery, a mage can't mess with another being's \u201ctemplate\u201d, whatever it is that makes it what it is. Making a Promethean was specifically called out as something that mages can't do; though when you think about it, that's merely an example of the general inability of magic to impose, remove, or alter templates.<br /> <br /> In theory, an archmaster with seven dots in the appropriate Arcana could use magic to create a Promethean. Oddly though, while Imperial Mysteries lists the Arcana needed for most of the other gamelines in publication at the time, it's silent on what's needed for Prometheans. Some have taken this as an indication that even Archmasters don't know how to create Prometheans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 12-16-2016, 04:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T13:04:26-08:00","id":1018195,"title":"","content":"Dataweaver: Very good point in your edit. However, it seems to me that the problem here might be that some people might object to the idea that mages can literally create characters from other games. Am I correct, or am I missing the point?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T13:07:02-08:00","id":1018196,"title":"","content":"So I was right...I have a feeling the designers were afraid mages would be too powerful compared to other splats if they didn't impose an artificial limitation...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T13:14:16-08:00","id":1018199,"title":"","content":"I don't think it's an artificial limitation. And magic can create characters from other games; but you have to enter archmaster territory to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 12-17-2016, 11:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T13:23:17-08:00","id":1018205,"title":"","content":"So... my idea doesn't work, do I understand this correctly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/373-infernal-teddy","name":"Infernal Teddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar373_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T13:28:58-08:00","id":1018206,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. In that case, both Isis and Inanna are Archmasters--a reasonable assumption, since both are worshipped as gods. Still, it troubles that an ordinary human with no supernatural traits can be a Demiurge, but a mage can't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T13:31:55-08:00","id":1018208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Infernal Teddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1018139-who-can-be-a-demiurge?p=1018205#post1018205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... my idea doesn't work, do I understand this correctly?</div> </div> </div> </div> If you want to stick to the rules as written, it doesn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T13:52:25-08:00","id":1018213,"title":"","content":"Damn <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Well, thanks for your help everyone... now, off to a new idea I suppose <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/373-infernal-teddy","name":"Infernal Teddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar373_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T14:03:51-08:00","id":1018217,"title":"","content":"You could always have the mage create a homunculus and bind his friend's ghost to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T14:09:48-08:00","id":1018218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Infernal Teddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1018139-who-can-be-a-demiurge#post1018139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been thinking about a pair of NPC's for my setting, one of whom has brought the other back from the dead. I originally thought of making the returned one a vampire, but then I thought of making the character a Promethean. Now I realize that the Created hardly if at all remember who the bodies were they were formed from, but I wonder - could a mage or an occultist be a demiurge? Could such a character act as demiurge to, say, an ulgan? If this question has already been answered somewhere, I apologize, I onlyown the 1st edition core bok.</div> </div> </div> </div>A mage can be a demiurge-but it's difficult.<br /> <br /> The Divine Fire requires a massive effort of will to be brought down and out. You might think that means mages would do well-but it requires an extreme, raw will, that the mages actually aren't comfortable with. It requires <i>desperation</i>, raw and bleeding awful desire, pure and simple-the sheer need to change, the sheer need for life, the visceral Has To that breaks worlds. Mages have will, but they also are creatures of insight and understanding over that level of pure feeling, using symbols and meaning all over the place, and that reliance on these things keeps them from that pure power needed to draw down the Divine Fire. The reason a mage needs to temporarily abandon their magic is because their magic, by it's nature, distracts and dampens their call for &quot;Has To Change&quot; with it's own call to &quot;Understand and Become&quot;.<br /> <br /> Your idea works-but it's going to be a Mystery for the mage unlike any they had previously, one that defies their normal conventions.<br /> <br /> I suppose the simple way to say it is that calling the Divine Fire is not really an act of Will so much as it is Want-a level of self-consuming Want that most people will not know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T14:36:44-08:00","id":1018227,"title":"","content":"First and foremost - <b>Remeber that Promethean is game about impossibility made possible.</b> It's even written in the 2E corebook:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PtC 2E, p.12</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prometheans are exceptions to many rules. They are splinters. They are things that don\u2019t quite fit, grotesque reminders of the struggle for humanity and the arcane weirdness of the Chronicles of Darkness. When reading this book, any time you see a declarative statement about the Created, please mentally append \u201cusually\u201d to the statement. Prometheans cannot sire or bear children\u2026 usually. Prometheans cause Disquiet in human beings\u2026usually. Prometheans become human at the end of the Pilgrimage\u2026usually.<br /> Promethean relies on strange, unique circumstances and once-in-a-billion occurrences, though, so if something happens in your chronicles that breaks the rules, that\u2019s entirely in keeping with the game\u2019s intent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now, to return to other posts...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Infernal Teddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1018139-who-can-be-a-demiurge?p=1018205#post1018205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... my idea doesn't work, do I understand this correctly?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it <i>can</i> work. Azoth is 'wish fulfilling obsession', in reality, so mage that want enough can spark the new life. It's just will be hailing from his Demiurge obsession, not his knowledge of Arcana. It was basically the idea of one of my Mage LARP player that run his Pygmalian Society member, wanting to create his own Galatea. With Supernal Magic he crafted her body out of marble, but then made whole ritual hailing simply from his obsession - and he make previous crafted marble body <i>alive</i>.<br /> <br /> In 2E RAW he would created Extempore Construct, but the most important fact is that mages CAN create sentient Prometheans - just it's 'sentience' and Pilgrimage is not hailing from Arcana. Mage, in reality, need to become conduit for Pyros to give real life to previous 'robot' being.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JulianMoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1018139-who-can-be-a-demiurge?p=1018206#post1018206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, it troubles that an ordinary human with no supernatural traits can be a Demiurge, but a mage can't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Khem, khem, khem - Supernatural creatures CAN create Prometheans. They just cannot make them <i>mass produced</i>, with their Gifts, Arcana, Contracts or whatever other power. Prometheans created by other supernatural are like 'once in a lifetime' events - but <i>are</i> possible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PtC 2E, p.38</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">More rarely, Extempore are created when some other power meddles in the Divine Fire. If a mage were to become sufficiently obsessed with the line between life and death to attempt to duplicate Victor Frankenstein\u2019s experiment or a werewolf tried to imbue a body with spiritual energy and reassemble it, as described in the myth of Tengri, the most likely result is a messy corpse or possibly a Firestorm.<b> If the would-be demiurge is somehow successful, however, the resulting creature is unlikely to be a \u201cnormal\u201d Promethean.</b> She will be touched by the energies of another world, tainted by an ancient curse, or otherwise burdened with something from beyond the Promethean experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again I stress - <b>Pyros is all about obsession</b> - if you are enough obsessed to create life, you <i>can</i> create Promethean, one way or another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-16-2016, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T07:23:00-08:00","id":1018451,"title":"","content":"ArcaneArts: Thank you! Now I understand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T18:39:17-08:00","id":1018637,"title":"","content":"Is it possible to play a demiurge as a minor template of some sort, like alchemists? (Well, alchemists aren't playable yet, but then I like the possibility of playing one)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T18:49:05-08:00","id":1018640,"title":"","content":"No template needed. A demiurge is a regular mortal. The only difference is that he's desperate enough to be able to succeed in creating a Promethean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T19:01:50-08:00","id":1018644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1018139-who-can-be-a-demiurge?p=1018640#post1018640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No template needed. A demiurge is a regular mortal. The only difference is that he's desperate enough to be able to succeed in creating a Promethean.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see. I guess then, for now, alchemists are the only type of humans perma-burned by the Fire?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T19:12:56-08:00","id":1018647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1018139-who-can-be-a-demiurge?p=1018644#post1018644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, I see. I guess then, for now, alchemists are the only type of humans perma-burned by the Fire?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. Demiurges put all their &quot;Has To Change&quot; into the lightning strike of creation-after that, <i>most</i> demiurges are temporarily satisfied, and probably spent on the subject.<br /> <br /> Alchemists are trying to hold that lightning a lot longer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T19:21:34-08:00","id":1018649,"title":"","content":"One could say that being Perma-burned is their defining quality, and what sets them apart from the other people who call themselves Alchemists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T22:56:33-08:00","id":1018705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1018139-who-can-be-a-demiurge?p=1018640#post1018640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No template needed. A demiurge is a regular mortal. The only difference is that he's desperate enough to be able to <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">succeed</span> in creating a Promethean.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI feel the need to point something out: Most non-Promethean Demiurges are NOT trying to make a Promethean. They are trying to make/resurrect a human. Making a Promethean is technically a <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">failure</span>. If a Mage wanted to restore someone to life, they have other methods. They might not ACTUALLY revive that person, but they COULD use Life to make a reasonable approximation of the persons body, and Mind to recreate something like the original's personality. Giving them a soul might be a little trickier, but can be accomplished with Death.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T23:02:03-08:00","id":1018706,"title":"","content":"Reviving the dead is only one motivation that a demiurge might have. Creating life is the one thing that all demiurges are desperate to achieve, but the reason for can vary greatly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T00:12:00-08:00","id":1018720,"title":"","content":"There's a lot of things that fit under the umbrella of &quot;I must defy the natural order of the world as revolves around this lump of material that bears resemblance to human form. Something Has To Change.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T00:33:57-08:00","id":1018725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1018139-who-can-be-a-demiurge?p=1018637#post1018637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible to play a demiurge as a minor template of some sort, like alchemists? (Well, alchemists aren't playable yet, but then I like the possibility of playing one)</div> </div> </div> </div>You can easily have Demiurga that is Alchemist. He is just more likely to conusme his creation for Pyros when Disquite will hit him. We basiclly done this variant in our game where earderly jewish (Al)chemist from MIT wanted to transfer his conciense to new and firm body of athlete student, ending in professors death and student returning as Promethean, with some residual memories of student AND Alchemist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T06:12:35-08:00","id":1019183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1018139-who-can-be-a-demiurge?p=1018647#post1018647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep. Demiurges put all their &quot;Has To Change&quot; into the lightning strike of creation-after that, <i>most</i> demiurges are temporarily satisfied, and probably spent on the subject.</div> </div> </div> </div>Back on the subject of mages for a moment, Awakenings can be triggered by witnessing big supernatural events, and making Promethean is a pretty big supernatural events. So a demiurge could have been an occult student before and a mage after, which would probably give them an interesting relationship with their creation.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}